d uk2026: Writing R Markdown documents in Stata
R Markdown, an extension of Pandoc Markdown, is promoted as a grand
d unified solution to writing computer-generated scientific
d documents. It inputs a text document, and outputs documents in
d formats .docx and/or .html and/or .pdf (via LaTeX). The output
d documents can contain publication-quality tables, graphics, and
d also equations (in formats .html or .pdf). Unsurprisingly, the 
d input text file can be generated using Stata, using the official
d Stata file command, together with the SSC packages listtab to
d make the tables and tfinsert to make the rest of the document. We
d demonstrate how this might be done.
d
d Author: Roger Newson
d Distribution-date: 06 September 2026
